.TH "frontend/node_modules/anymatch Directory Reference" 3 "Version 0.1" "Chat-ME!" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/anymatch Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Javascript module to match a string against a regular expression, glob, string, or function that takes the string as an argument and returns a truthy or falsy value\&. The matcher can also be an array of any or all of these\&. Useful for allowing a very flexible user-defined config to define things like file paths\&.

.PP
\fBNote: This module has Bash-parity, please be aware that Windows-style backslashes are not supported as separators\&. See https://github.com/micromatch/micromatch#backslashes for more information\&.\fP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install anymatch
.fi
.PP
.SS "anymatch(matchers, testString, [returnIndex], [options])"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBmatchers\fP: (\fIArray|String|RegExp|Function\fP) String to be directly matched, string with glob patterns, regular expression test, function that takes the testString as an argument and returns a truthy value if it should be matched, or an array of any number and mix of these types\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBtestString\fP: (\fIString|Array\fP) The string to test against the matchers\&. If passed as an array, the first element of the array will be used as the \fRtestString\fP for non-function matchers, while the entire array will be applied as the arguments for function matchers\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBoptions\fP: (\fIObject\fP [optional]_) Any of the \fRpicomatch\fP options\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBreturnIndex\fP: (\fIBoolean [optional]\fP) If true, return the array index of the first matcher that that testString matched, or -1 if no match, instead of a boolean result\&.
.PP

.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const anymatch = require('anymatch');

const matchers = [ 'path/to/file\&.js', 'path/anyjs/**/*\&.js', /foo\&.js$/, string => string\&.includes('bar') && string\&.length > 10 ] ;

anymatch(matchers, 'path/to/file\&.js'); // true
anymatch(matchers, 'path/anyjs/baz\&.js'); // true
anymatch(matchers, 'path/to/foo\&.js'); // true
anymatch(matchers, 'path/to/bar\&.js'); // true
anymatch(matchers, 'bar\&.js'); // false

// returnIndex = true
anymatch(matchers, 'foo\&.js', {returnIndex: true}); // 2
anymatch(matchers, 'path/anyjs/foo\&.js', {returnIndex: true}); // 1

// any picomatc

// using globs to match directories and their children
anymatch('node_modules', 'node_modules'); // true
anymatch('node_modules', 'node_modules/somelib/index\&.js'); // false
anymatch('node_modules/**', 'node_modules/somelib/index\&.js'); // true
anymatch('node_modules/**', '/absolute/path/to/node_modules/somelib/index\&.js'); // false
anymatch('**/node_modules/**', '/absolute/path/to/node_modules/somelib/index\&.js'); // true

const matcher = anymatch(matchers);
['foo\&.js', 'bar\&.js']\&.filter(matcher);  // [ 'foo\&.js' ]
anymatch master* ❯
.fi
.PP
.SS "anymatch(matchers)"
You can also pass in only your matcher(s) to get a curried function that has already been bound to the provided matching criteria\&. This can be used as an \fRArray#filter\fP callback\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
var matcher = anymatch(matchers);

matcher('path/to/file\&.js'); // true
matcher('path/anyjs/baz\&.js', true); // 1

['foo\&.js', 'bar\&.js']\&.filter(matcher); // ['foo\&.js']
.fi
.PP
.SH "Changelog"
.PP
\fRSee release notes page on GitHub\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBv3\&.0:\fP Removed \fRstartIndex\fP and \fRendIndex\fP arguments\&. Node 8\&.x-only\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBv2\&.0:\fP \fRmicromatch\fP moves away from minimatch-parity and inline with Bash\&. This includes handling backslashes differently (see https://github.com/micromatch/micromatch#backslashes for more information)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBv1\&.2:\fP anymatch uses \fRmicromatch\fP for glob pattern matching\&. Issues with glob pattern matching should be reported directly to the \fRmicromatch issue tracker\fP\&.
.PP
